  "description": "EQECUB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C145 H155 Br10 Cd6 N15 O50 Sm4 4+,C1 H4 O1,4(N1 O3 1-),C1 H2 Cl2. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Cd1 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd2 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Cd3 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd4 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Sm4 (Sm) has 9 O neighbors; Cd5 (Cd) has 3 O neighbors; Cd6 (Cd) has 5 O neighbors; Cd7? (Cd) has 0 O neighbors; Cd8? (Cd) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a chain with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.660-4.225 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.92-112.52°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C147H161Br10Cd6Cl2N19O63Sm4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
